dts: rk3576: give the NPU power domains their BIU resets

The NPU0 and NPU1 domains come out of a cold power-on with the bus
interface in an undefined state, and the first access hangs. The pmdomain
driver now pulses a domain's resets between releasing idle and restoring
QoS, so name the BIU resets for the two domains that need it.

Inert without the driver side (patch 0020): domains that declare no resets
behave as they did.

Taken from Jiaxing Hu's RFC v4 5/6, whose power-domain hunk otherwise
matches what patch 0012 already carries here.

Signed-off-by: Isaiah DeRose-Wilson <isaiahdw@gmail.com>

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576.dtsi
@@ -1153,6 +1153,7 @@
 								 <&cru CLK_RKNN_DSU0>,
 								 <&cru ACLK_RKNN_CBUF>,
 								 <&cru HCLK_RKNN_CBUF>;
+							resets = <&cru SRST_A_RKNN0_BIU>;
 							pm_qos = <&qos_npu_m0>;
 							#power-domain-cells = <0>;
 						};
@@ -1163,6 +1164,7 @@
 								 <&cru CLK_RKNN_DSU0>,
 								 <&cru ACLK_RKNN_CBUF>,
 								 <&cru HCLK_RKNN_CBUF>;
+							resets = <&cru SRST_A_RKNN1_BIU>;
 							pm_qos = <&qos_npu_m1>;
 							#power-domain-cells = <0>;
 						};
